{:edb/db-before-t 1309 :edb/db-after-t 1310 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534622 50 #inst "2026-10-12T05:01:52.700Z" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186194525 1078 #edb/ref 17592186194527 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186198415 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429803 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186198415 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429804 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186198416 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429800 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186198416 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429801 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186198418 1038 #edb/ref 17592186429802 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186198499 1050 1260.0 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186198649 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186198649 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D = {(x, y): - 1 \\le x \\le 2, 0 \\le y \\le 3}$.\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y = 3$." 13194139534622 17592186045417 false] [17592186198649 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=3.$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186198649 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $y=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-3|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}(8-(-1))(3-0) \\\\  & =9k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=\\frac{M}{9}{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{M}{9}{x}^{2}|y-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{M}{9}{x}^{2}(y-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}({\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{3}(y-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{-1}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y-3)^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}(8-(-1))\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(0+27)] \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{9}\\cdot 3\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429770 1080 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429770 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429770 1083 #uuid "0aa6bf74-d5a3-5958-b981-8c521b9d0f63" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429771 1080 "\\frac{27M}{10}" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429771 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429771 1083 #uuid "0e7a9644-cba7-5f24-9b3d-6e9c2c8bc75f" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429772 1080 "\\frac{37M}{10}" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429772 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429772 1083 #uuid "1b5a5e39-8315-5424-90e3-fcb80169363e" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429