 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429793 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429798 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429794 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429798 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429798 1077 "selection" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429798 1078 #edb/ref 17592186429793 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429798 1079 #uuid "959d5a6f-4d25-59a7-adf2-d4fcda6ed2ca" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429781 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429782 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429783 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429786 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429799 1075 #edb/ref 17592186429790 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429799 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429799 1077 "selection" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429799 1078 #edb/ref 17592186429781 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429799 1079 #uuid "d6b5455b-decf-5778-8118-b924e2fb8500" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429800 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429795 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429800 1069 "q-163620" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429800 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429800 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=1.$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429800 1072 #uuid "3deb3a9e-9ac5-5836-9b00-e8c458f26b4c" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429800 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 1=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{M}{2}|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{M}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}({\\int }_{1}^{3}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(x-1)^{3}]_{1}^{3}\\cdot {[y]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(\\frac{1}{3}(3-1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(1-1)^{3})\\cdot (2-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(\\frac{8}{3}-0)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{4M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429801 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429796 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429801 1069 "q-163646" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429801 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429801 1071 "![](images/c4/c46bf82e7609abe56e9e65ef0e81e21438a67e849d80d560baff5ab0c90bde11.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=x+2$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{9}{2},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429801 1072 #uuid "428bf855-ba76-5902-a5ae-83ea9f5f66d0" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429801 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x+2\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/f4/f48cd4e22c083d6c05ba9908a788402b05d839fea710a7328297d9e392e3636e.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{2M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x-2)^{2}[y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x+2-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}-{x}^{4}+5{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-4x+8\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{4}-2{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+8x]}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}[(-\\frac{32}{5}+20-16-8+16)-(\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{5}{4}+2-2-8)] \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}(\\frac{28}{5}-(-\\frac{131}{20})) \\\\  & =\\frac{27M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429802 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429798 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429802 1069 "q-163716" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429802 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429802 1071 "![](images/e0/e0fe5ad37bd641a7d88eb75629f243d383f392230b86be723556d63cedbd8f95.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the half-ellipses $y=\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}$ and $y=\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}},$ and the lines $x=\\pm 1.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=1.$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429802 1072 #uuid "7e9fa766-851a-51de-9b68-1e331e71ab1a" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429802 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/8a/8ac2ade388bcc0dee28b1a5bbaf0807ae253c0c785b9a63978014e873fe8a1ce.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k|y|=ky,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(9-3{x}^{2}-(3-{x}^{2}))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(6-2{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(3-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[3x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{16k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=ky=\\frac{3}{16}My.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\frac{3}{16}My|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\frac{3}{16}My(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}y(x-1)^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x-1)^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{\\sqrt{3-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-3{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x-1)^{2}(3-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-6x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-3{x}^{2}+3x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M(-\\frac{2}{5}+0+\\frac{4}{3}-0+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}M\\cdot \\frac{104}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{13M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429803 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429799 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429803 1069 "q-163506" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429803 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429803 1071 "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x+4y.$ Find the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $x=1.$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429803 1072 #uuid "83ed0974-8a48-5d4e-bd56-80ccf4096ca0" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429803 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+4y)|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x+4y)(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x(x-1)^{2}+4y(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2xy(x-1)^{2}+2{y}^{2}(x-1)^{2}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4x(x-1)^{2}+8(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}(4x+8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{3}-12x+8\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}-6{x}^{2}+8x]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(1-6+8)-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429804 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429797 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429804 1069 "q-163567" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429804 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429804 1071 "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x+1.$ Find the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=1.$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429804 1072 #uuid "f97fcac8-5f6e-54a6-8dcf-90235edee60f" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true] [17592186429804 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-1|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+1)|y-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+1)(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{2}(y-1)^{2}]}_{-1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{9}{2}(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3(y-1)^{3}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534622 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0aa6bf74-d5a3-5958-b981-8c521b9d0f63" 17592186429770 "answer-0e7a9644-cba7-5f24-9b3d-6e9c2c8bc75f" 17592186429771 "answer-1b5a5e39-8315-5424-90e3-fcb80169363e" 17592186429772 "answer-1c4ddd67-fd42-5465-8f14-15bc7de65c38" 17592186429773 "answer-2576a0ad-5174-5b7c-908a-b2315e46651c" 17592186429774 "answer-3a3d0166-0a75-5d0f-a9c3-7e41f234b7a7" 17592186429775 "answer-442982b4-7b77-52e3-a087-62e393e45551" 17592186429776 "answer-454fa18f-24d7-52fc-8e1c-cc51cd180608" 17592186429777 "answer-537b792d-49e0-59d8-9a68-d554ec233fc2" 17592186429778 "answer-574e0cf2-988e-5404-aeca-d14f66a34d9e" 17592186429779 "answer-605abb0a-980f-51cf-8efd-a3f81544604b" 17592186429780 "answer-7b922d65-9076-5bf1-85bd-f0dd7d4739b9" 17592186429781 "answer-89b9b462-0fd9-55dd-bace-35957f322894" 17592186429782 "answer-93cbd1b5-025e-5265-b16d-b3df6eec8d49" 17592186429783 "answer-9519e710-1736-538f-8233-3e723e4a4632" 17592186429784 "answer-a653fce9-385c-5f7b-905b-3885997f91cc" 17592186429785 "answer-ad2aedf6-5bca-5e95-938e-57e898e41618" 17592186429786 "answer-b5385549-d2b7-57f1-8393-8762fd9a0e6b" 17592186429787 "answer-ba09df7c-c245-55b5-903d-5b483622362c" 17592186429788 "answer-bd0f3239-8d4d-5e66-8e71-e8118a1d4143" 17592186429789 "answer-c385ea81-4ec1-5db5-9df3-f5c6b32521d4" 17592186429790 "answer-c6c5441f-500c-59c1-887d-2e0827473808" 17592186429791 "answer-d7737f7f-f77c-53ee-9ece-26a0c8e6e85e" 17592186429792 "answer-f759f521-9b31-5892-8aad-88389b051c93" 17592186429793 "answer-fcd9e27b-3c64-5b4a-9fc0-50a3d3edc345" 1